course: dictionary
lesson: 9828
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sweetness is a noun, and it is uncountable. We talk about sweetness as a quality that something or someone has, so you say «a little sweetness» or «much sweetness», not «two sweetnesses». The same word can have several meanings, so the words around it show which one you need.
explain: Read «the sweetness of his own little home again». Sweetness here is not about sugar. The Mole has been away, and home is a pleasant feeling he is happy to have back, so sweetness means that pleasant quality.
explain: Now read «the acid and fizz cover up the sweetness». The acid and fizz hide something, and the thing being hidden is the taste of sugar. Swap in the meaning: «the acid and fizz cover up the taste of sugar» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Sweetness is a noun, and it is uncountable.
fact: «Sweetness» can mean the taste of sugar or honey, or simply being sweet.
fact: «Sweetness» can also mean kindness, gentleness and a pleasant nature.
fact: A pleasant sound or smell can have sweetness too, as in «the sweetness of a song».
fact: As a pet name, «sweetness» is informal and is used to speak to someone you love.
exercise: In «the sweetness of his own little home again», what does sweetness mean? | The taste of sugar | A sharp, sour smell | A loud noise from the river | *The pleasant feeling of being back where you belong
exercise: In «the acid and fizz cover up the sweetness», what is being hidden? | *The taste of sugar | The cold temperature of the drink | The bubbles in the glass | The name of the drink
exercise: A teacher says, «Her sweetness made everyone feel welcome.» What does sweetness mean? | A bright colour on her coat | A loud and bossy voice | Sugar in her tea | *Kindness and a gentle nature
test: Which sentence uses sweetness correctly as an uncountable noun? | She was very sweetness in the morning. | She spoke to the little ones with great sweetnesses. | *She spoke to the little ones with great sweetness. | Her sweetnesses were many this week.
test: In «Good night, sweetness», what does sweetness mean? | A smell of flowers | A sound like a bell | *A loving name for someone you care about | The taste of sugar
exam: Which meaning fits best in «the sweetness of the song drifted through the open window»? | The taste of sugar | *A pleasant quality of a sound | Being unkind to others | A sharp smell from the kitchen
